{"name":"Weathered Saddle","hex":"#b5745c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"weathered","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Worn by weather, as of rocks, stone, etc.","Made slightly sloping, so as to throw off water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of weather"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weathered"},{"term":"saddle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A seat for a rider, typically made of leather and raised in the front and rear, placed on the back of a horse or other animal, and secured by a strap around the animal's body.\n\nA similar implement used to secure goods to animals; a packsaddle.\nSynonym of harness saddle (“the part of a harness which supports the weight of poles or shafts attaching a vehicle to a horse or other animal”).\nA cushion used as a seat in a cart or other vehicle.\nThe immovable seat of a bicycle, motorcycle, or similar vehicle.\n\nChiefly preceded by the: horse-riding as an activity or occupation.\n\nSynonym of saddle brown (“a medium brown colour, like that of saddle leather”).","A similar implement used to secure goods to animals; a packsaddle."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put a saddle (noun sense 1) on (an animal).\n\nTo put (something) on to another thing like a saddle on an animal.\n\n\nTo enter (a trained horse) into a race.\n Chiefly followed by with: to burden or encumber (someone) with some problem or responsibility.","To put a saddle (noun sense 1) on (an animal)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/saddle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Weathered","blocks":[{"text":"Weathered is the third studio album by American rock band Creed, released on November 20, 2001. It was the last Creed album to be released until Full Circle in October 2009, as Creed disbanded in June 2004. Weathered is the only Creed album to be recorded as a trio, as bassist Brian Marshall departed in August 2000, with guitarist Mark Tremonti taking over the bass guitar part during recording. Tremonti and vocalist Scott Stapp wrote most of the material for the album during a three-week period in late 2000, following their successful tour to support their second album, Human Clay. Manager Jeff Hanson once again paired the band with long-time producer John Kurzweg, who rented out a private residence/recording studio in Ocoee, Florida owned by Jay Stanley, where the band set up a studio inside to record the album. Recording sessions for the album began in July 2001 and took four months to complete."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a2/Weathered_Main_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weathered","wikidata":"Q2321182"},{"title":"Saddle","blocks":[{"text":"A saddle is a supportive structure for a rider of an animal, fastened to an animal's back by a girth. The most common type is equestrian. However, specialized saddles have been created for oxen, camels and other animals. The trade of making saddles is saddlery."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Saddle_with_shabrack_according_to_tradition_linked_with_Hetman_Miko%C5%82aj_Hieronim_Sieniawski.jpg/330px-Saddle_with_shabrack_according_to_tradition_linked_with_Hetman_Miko%C5%82aj_Hieronim_Sieniawski.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saddle","wikidata":"Q192249"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/81/Weathered_Alternate_Cover.jpg/250px-Weathered_Alternate_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/81/Weathered_Alternate_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/81/Weathered_Alternate_Cover.jpg/250px-Weathered_Alternate_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Alternate cover artwork for Weathered with the enlarged solid white wordmark and album title, and Mark Tremonti's head carved facing to the right.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWeathered_Alternate_Cover.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/StubbenTristan.jpg/500px-StubbenTristan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/StubbenTristan.jpg/1280px-StubbenTristan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/StubbenTristan.jpg/500px-StubbenTristan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A dressage-style English saddle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStubbenTristan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Yisaddle.JPG/500px-Yisaddle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Yisaddle.JPG/1280px-Yisaddle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Yisaddle.JPG/500px-Yisaddle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A saddle with lacquer overlay from the Yi ethnic minority province in Yunnan, China","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYisaddle.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Alvin_G._Davis_Saddle%2C_Post%2C_TX_IMG_1729.JPG/500px-Alvin_G._Davis_Saddle%2C_Post%2C_TX_IMG_1729.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Alvin_G._Davis_Saddle%2C_Post%2C_TX_IMG_1729.JPG/1280px-Alvin_G._Davis_Saddle%2C_Post%2C_T